ry": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [69921, 70517]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [70518, 71117]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [71118, 71717]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [71718, 72317]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [72318, 72917]}]}", "latency_ms": 22, "tokens_before": 36233, "tokens_after": 36233, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_4046bc34", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1010, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 883], "window": [65717, 75317], "confidence": 0.62, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "The only directed route from 1010 to 883 in the window is 1010->66->1952->1090->729->883, and its events are ordered forward in time: 1010's lone event and 66's and 1952's events all sit in [69921,70517], 1090's outgoing event in [70518,71117], and 883's first inbound event after that. The tight bucketing (<=600) of the first hops and the immediate adjacency of the next indicate a genuine time-respecting cascade rather than mere volume or static connectivity (1010 fires only once among 1951 events; the alternative 1209 branch is unreachable from 1010). The only unverified link is the exact delay on 729->883, hence moderate confidence."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure (time-ignored):** 1010 has exactly one out-edge, to 66 (step_03, step_11). 883 is only ever contacted by 729 and 1209 (step_04, step_08). 1209's in-neighbours (149, 296, 1542) do not appear in 1010's reachable set (step_10), so the only candidate route is via 729, whose sole in-neighbour is 1090 (step_09). From the k-hop edge list (step_05): 66\u21921952, 1952\u21921090, plus 1090\u2192729\u2192883. So the unique directed chain is **1010\u219266\u21921952\u21921090\u2192729\u2192883**.\n\n**Timing:** \n- 1010's single event lies in [69921, 70517] (step_07, step_12).\n- 66 has 2 events in [69921, 70517] (the incoming one from 1010 plus one outgoing) (step_14).\n- 1952 has both of its events in the same [69921, 70517] bucket and none afterwards (step_15).\n- 1090 has one event in [69921, 70517] and one in the *next* bucket [70518, 71117] (step_16).\n- 883's first event falls in [70518, 72917] (step_13), i.e. after 1090's outgoing event.\n\nEvery hop of the unique path advances monotonically in time, with the first four hops compressed into a \u2264600-unit bucket and the hand-off to 1090\u2192729 in the immediately adjacent bucket. This is a forward-flowing chain, not a coincidence of high volume (1010 fires only once in 1951 events \u2014 step_01, step_02).\n\n**Residual uncertainty:** the final hop 729\u2192883 is only localised to a 2400-unit bucket, so the \u2264600 gap on that last link is inferred rather than directly verified.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_4046bc34\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 883],\n  \"window\": [65717, 75317],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The only directed route from 1010 to 883 in the window is 1010->66->1952->1090->729->883, and its events are ordered forward in time: 1010's lone event and 66's and 1952's events all sit in [69921,70517], 1090's outgoing event in [70518,71117], and 883's first inbound event after that. The tight bucketing (<=600) of the first hops and the immediate adjacency of the next indicate a genuine time-respecting cascade rather than mere volume or static connectivity (1010 fires only once among 1951 events; the alternative 1209 branch is unreachable from 1010). The only unverified link is the exact delay on 729->883, hence moderate confidence.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 44721, "total_output_tokens": 6849, "total_tokens": 51570, "total_latency_ms": 94513, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}